Squinch system pack
===================

Icon artwork in `icons/` comes from Lucide (https://lucide.dev), released under
the ISC licence. The full licence text is in LICENSE-ICONS.txt.

Copyright (c) for portions of Lucide are held by Cole Bemis 2013-2022 as part of
Feather (MIT). All other copyright (c) for Lucide are held by Lucide Contributors
2022.

ISC permits use, copying, modification and distribution with the copyright
notice retained, so unlike the cloud packs there is no no-derivatives
constraint here. The files in `icons/` are nonetheless copied **verbatim**, at
Lucide's own 2px stroke weight: keeping them byte-faithful means the set stays a
single coherent hand, and `npm run fetch` can pick up upstream fixes without
re-applying local edits. Theme treatment (the neutral plate, the currentColor
tint) happens at render time in @squinch/core, never here.

This is the `sys` pack — the generic half of Squinch's icon vocabulary, for the
things no cloud vendor draws: servers, racks, laptops, factories, network gear,
and plain shapes for when nothing else fits. It resolves without a `pack`
statement. Curated by role rather than vendored whole; Lucide ships over 2,000
icons and the list in scripts/fetch.ts is the subset that earns its place in an
architecture diagram. Add an id, run `npm run fetch`, commit the result.

